        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "But like the word clear, the words choppy, disorganized, and connected refer not to the words on the page but to how they make us feel. What is it about the arrangement of words in 1a that makes us feel we are moving through it in fits and starts? Why does 1b seem to flow more easily? We base those judgments on two aspects of word order:",
